=== ffm
Usage:
  ffm [command]

Available Commands:
  backup      Archive a bench's site into a single restorable file
  clean-logs  Delete old log table rows to reclaim database space
  create      Create and start a new Frappe bench
  dashboard   Web dashboard for managing Frappe benches
  delete      Delete a bench and all its data
  domain      Manage extra hostnames that route to a bench
  ffc         Generate Frappe API keys and configure ffc inside a bench
  list        List all managed benches
  logs        Stream logs from a bench (all services or one)
  proxy       Manage the shared Traefik reverse proxy (sitename.localhost routing)
  reconcile   Apply this ffm version's templates to an existing bench without losing data
  recreate    Delete a bench and provision it again from saved settings
  restart     Restart a bench (stop then start)
  restore     Rebuild a bench from a backup archive
  set-proxy   Configure a bench to run behind a reverse proxy
  shell       Open an interactive shell inside a bench container
  start       Start a stopped bench
  status      Show per-container status for a bench
  stop        Stop a running bench (containers remain, data preserved)
  tunnel      Expose a bench over a secure public URL via a VPS tunnel
  update      Update ffm to the latest version
  version     Print the ffm version

Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

Use "ffm [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== ffm backup
Usage:
  ffm backup [name] [flags]
  ffm backup [command]

Examples:
  ffm backup
  ffm backup mybench
  ffm backup mybench --out ~/archives
  ffm backup mybench --no-files --label "before the v16 upgrade"
  ffm backup mybench --vendor-apps my_app

Available Commands:
  list        List backup archives, newest first
  prune       Apply a bench's retention policy to its scheduled archives now
  run-due     Back up every bench whose schedule is due (run by the hourly system job)
  schedule    Back a bench up automatically, keeping a bounded set of archives
  scheduler   Manage the hourly system job that runs scheduled backups

Flags:
      --label string          Short note recorded in the archive
      --no-files              Skip file attachments and archive the database only
      --out string            Directory to write the archive into, or an explicit path ending in .tar (default: ~/frappe/_backups/<bench>/, overridable with $FFM_BACKUPS_DIR)
      --skip-space-check      Write the archive without checking free disk space first
      --vendor-apps strings   Also archive the source of these apps (comma-separated, or 'all'), uncommitted changes included. Apps that cannot be cloned back are archived regardless

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

Use "ffm backup [command] --help" for more information about a command.

