      --verbose           Show docker compose output

=== ffm backup schedule
Usage:
  ffm backup schedule [bench] [flags]

Examples:
  ffm backup schedule mybench --every 24h
  ffm backup schedule mybench --every 1h --files weekly
  ffm backup schedule mybench --every weekly --keep 3
  ffm backup schedule mybench --off
  ffm backup schedule

Flags:
      --every string      Interval: 1h, 6h, 24h, 168h (whole hours), or hourly/daily/weekly (default "24h")
      --files string      Include attachments: every-run, daily, weekly or never
      --json              With no bench: print every schedule as machine-readable JSON (schema ffm.schedules/v1)
      --keep int          Keep N archives of the tier matching --every
      --keep-daily int    Keep the newest archive of each of the last N days
      --keep-hourly int   Keep the newest archive of each of the last N hours
      --keep-weekly int   Keep the newest archive of each of the last N weeks
      --no-install        Save the schedule without installing or removing the hourly system job
      --off               Stop scheduled backups for the bench (archives are kept)

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

