=== ffm tunnel
Usage:
  ffm tunnel [name] [flags]
  ffm tunnel [command]

Available Commands:
  server      Manage VPS tunnel server profiles

Flags:
      --allow-default-password   Publish the bench even though it still has the default admin password
      --off                      Disable the tunnel and restore direct-access Frappe settings
      --print                    Print the rendered frpc.toml without applying anything
      --server string            Tunnel server profile name (default: configured default)
      --subdomain string         Public subdomain slug (default: bench name)

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

Use "ffm tunnel [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== ffm tunnel server
Usage:
  ffm tunnel server [flags]
  ffm tunnel server [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add a new tunnel server profile
  remove      Remove a tunnel server profile
  set         Edit an existing tunnel server profile
  use         Set the default tunnel server profile

Flags:
      --json           Print machine-readable JSON (schema ffm.tunnel-servers/v1)
      --show-secrets   Include auth tokens in --json output

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

Use "ffm tunnel server [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== ffm tunnel server add
Usage:
  ffm tunnel server add <name> [flags]

Flags:
      --base-domain string   Base domain for tunnels, e.g. tunnel.example.com
      --host string          VPS hostname or IP address
      --no-tls               Disable TLS on the frp control channel
      --port string          frps bind port (control channel), e.g. 7000
      --token string         frps auth token

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

=== ffm tunnel server remove
Usage:
  ffm tunnel server remove <name> [flags]

Aliases:
  remove, rm, delete

Flags:
  -y, --yes   Remove without asking for confirmation

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

